1
00:00:01,640 --> 00:00:06,770
Read, write decimal

2
00:00:06,770 --> 00:00:16,660
We learn together how to read, how to write decimal via following examples:

3
00:00:17,770 --> 00:00:32,770
Example 1: Decimal number 528,103 is read: five hundred twenty-eight point one zero three.

4
00:00:33,550 --> 00:00:47,930
Example 2: Decimal number consisting of twenty-three ones, one tenth, seven hundredths written is: 23,17

5
00:00:48,600 --> 00:00:58,150
Remember: To read a decimal number, we read in order from high place to low place:

6
00:00:58,150 --> 00:01:09,750
First read whole part, read "comma", then read decimal part.

7
00:01:10,240 --> 00:01:19,330
To write a decimal number, we write in order from high place to low place:

8
00:01:19,330 --> 00:01:33,570
First write whole part, write "comma", then write decimal part.

9
00:01:34,110 --> 00:01:39,530
Tell how to read decimal number below

10
00:01:39,530 --> 00:01:50,880
Decimal number 105,407 is read: One hundred five point four zero seven

11
00:01:50,880 --> 00:01:59,000
Fill in blank

12
00:01:59,480 --> 00:02:04,200
Tell how to write decimal number below:

13
00:02:04,200 --> 00:02:16,330
Decimal number consisting of two thousand zero hundred eight ones, three hundredths written is: 2008,03

14
00:02:18,080 --> 00:02:25,420
Fill in blank

